<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Issue #26-MED-008 — APNs environment entitlement.

      `aps-environment` is the Apple-required entitlement for push
      notifications. Without it, APNs registration fails silently and
      Firebase Messaging never receives a real token on iOS — the app
      thinks it's registered but the OS strips the request at the
      entitlement layer.

      `development` value matches debug + TestFlight builds; the App
      Store production build flips to `production` automatically when
      the App ID's Push Notifications capability is enabled in
      App Store Connect (Xcode build settings handle the swap).

      TODO(release-eng): confirm the App ID has Push Notifications
      enabled in the Apple Developer Portal. If not, this entitlement
      will cause a code-signing failure at build time, which is the
      right fail-loud behaviour — better than silent registration
      failure at runtime.
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>development</string>
    <!--
      Universal Links for OAuth/SAML callbacks. Instead of the public
      custom URL scheme (jp.willen.saso://) which any installed app can
      claim, the IdP/auth host issues an https:// callback that iOS
      verifies against an apple-app-site-association (AASA) JSON hosted
      at https://auth.willen.jp/.well-known/apple-app-site-association.

      TODO(infra): publish the AASA file at the IdP host with this app's
      Team ID + bundle identifier before flipping the SSO flow to use
      https callbacks. Until then, the custom scheme in Info.plist is the
      only callback path that works — kept as compatibility fallback.
      See docs/release/applinks.md for the AASA body, hosting requirements,
      verification checklist, and the iOS-side cleanup steps to run once
      the infra publish is live (issue #144).
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>applinks:auth.willen.jp</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
